## 31-Oct-7:50am-PST/PDT — Grok: the standing crashes are closed

The six race_stash records and the two board_mail records that were still on file were the same two faults. A resend and a direct deliver could both send one outbox record; the send and the move into sent/ now share one lock per key. The board subject is read with the shared grammar, so a unit separator is part of the id and the message is handled, and a board key that is not a task id is not loaded and not offered. Replayed at this tree: board_mail 1 promoted and 1 redundant, race_stash 1 promoted and 5 redundant, none still crash. The measurement hold is unchanged.

